# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# next.js
/.next/
/out/
next-env.d.ts

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# hosts
.vercel
# netlify: local link state and build cache, written by `netlify link`/`deploy`
.netlify/

# test output
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/.lighthouseci/
/coverage/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Playwright visual baselines.
#
# These are the expected result rather than a build product, so committing them
# is the usual practice — but they are ~1.5 MB each and 21 MB in total, which
# is more than this repository should carry for a site. The consequence is that
# `npm run test:e2e` writes fresh baselines on a machine that has none, so the
# visual specs assert "this rendered" rather than "this did not change".
# Everything that a screenshot would otherwise pin — contrast in both themes,
# window chrome, layout overflow, focus behaviour — is asserted explicitly by
# the other specs, which do run everywhere.
**/*-snapshots/

# Ad-hoc capture output from tests/e2e
/capture/

# macOS / editors
.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Copied from the repository by scripts/sync-assets.mjs before every build.
/public/generated/
